[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661110391","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102898#issuecomment-2661110391","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102898","id":2661110391,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6enVJ3","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T21:24:48Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T21:24:48Z","body":"Looks right to me. Except that for local variables we should infer the exact type at each point in the function (this is not implemented). Then GDScript would be able to determine that a variable with declared type `A` has a value of subtype `B` at that point. However, for class members such inference is not possible, so the warning is correct.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661110391/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661410979","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102898#issuecomment-2661410979","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102898","id":2661410979,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eoeij","user":{"login":"monty-c","id":168653940,"node_id":"U_kgDOCg10dA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168653940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c","html_url":"https://github.com/monty-c","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/monty-c/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-16T12:31:46Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T12:31:46Z","body":"Yeah, actually having thought about it further it makes decent sense. If I'm confident enough that `make_node()` is going to give me a `Node3D` so far as to access `position` on it, then I may as well have assigned the instance to a variable of type `B`, or cast it to `B` inline, since `A.make_node()` only promises that it'll give me `Node` - regardless of what it might be cooking up in the function body.\n\nI'm curious about what you mean about the distinction for local variables though.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661410979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661437557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102898#issuecomment-2661437557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102898","id":2661437557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eolB1","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-16T13:40:13Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T13:40:13Z","body":"> I'm curious about what you mean about the distinction for local variables though.\n\nLocal variables cannot be reassigned from outside the function, so we could analyze the control flow and infer the exact types of the local variable at each point in the function. While this is not possible for class members, their values ​​can be changed by any call with a side effect (there is no `pure` qualifier in GDScript, etc.). Additionally, a class member can have a setter or be changed via the debugger. Compare:\n\n```gdscript\nvar instance: A\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n    instance = B.new() # `instance` is `B` (there is no setter).\n    side_effect() # Can reassign `instance`.\n    print(instance) # `instance` is `A`.\n```\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n    var instance: A = B.new() # `instance` is `B`.\n    side_effect() # Cannot reassign `instance`.\n    print(instance) # `instance` is `B`.\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661437557/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]